name: Direct local Scan settles source drift before committing observations
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN SEMGREP_AGENT_TOKEN
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART baseline
require-live-snap: 30 1 finding | baseline-scan
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Owned source settlement marker | baseline-observation
submit: decision deferred Owned static marker needs operator review
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | deferred-observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART deferred
ask: Does the actual direct local scanner retain one labeled signal and a clearly scripted deferral without claiming a verified vulnerability?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare-drift
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART release-with-edit
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
require-live-snap: 30 Source could not be verified | partial-source-receipt
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-after-drift
expect-not: not observed in a later covered run
resize: 160x48
live-snap: retained-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: retained-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: retained-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: retained-60x20
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 F-0001 · FINDING | finding-reader
resize: 40x12
live-snap: retained-40x12
expect: F-0001
expect: PgUp/PgDn read
ask: Does source drift retain the prior decision and finding identity, with usable reading controls at all six terminal sizes?
resize: 120x36
keys: q
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Displayed Scan: partial | partial-history-report
expect: Scope: workspace history
expect: Scan receipt does not establish complete repository coverage.
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial-report
ask: Does the direct Scan Report disclose partial work and source uncertainty without treating finding review completeness as repository coverage?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART stable
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART complete
require-live-snap: 30 0 findings | stable-scan
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | retained-after-complete
ask: Does a separately requested stable empty scan retain the earlier observation, partial run and deferral without declaring a fix?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | recovered-review
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/direct_scan_settlement.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: After no-color restart, are all three direct scan outcomes and the retained decision readable without new work or source execution?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
